{"question": "Sorrento Therapeutics terminated its phase 2 COVI-MSC trial NCT04903327. Why did it stop, and were the results ever posted or published?", "report": {"answer": ["The registry states that Sorrento Therapeutics terminated its Phase 2 COVI-MSC trial NCT04903327 because slow enrollment made it unable to reach enrollment targets.", "No formal results have been posted to the registry, and no results publication has been found in PubMed or Europe PMC.", "While the sponsor filed several SEC 8-K disclosures mentioning the COVI-MSC therapy, these filings do not state a reason for the trial's termination or report its clinical results."], "evidence": ["Trial NCT04903327 began on 2021-11-16 and reached primary completion on 2022-08-29 with an enrollment of 43 patients.", "The trial reached completion on 2022-11-23 and has an overall status of terminated.", "No results have been posted on ClinicalTrials.gov, where results were due on 2023-08-29.", "No results publication was found in PubMed or Europe PMC.", "Five publications linked to the trial were found to only mention it as a review or systematic review without containing primary clinical results.", "Sorrento Therapeutics filed SEC 8-K disclosures on February 22, 2023, March 20, 2023, and March 31, 2023, that mention COVI-MSC only as a trademark or pipeline program.", "The drug COVI-MSC has never received FDA approval."], "differences": ["The SEC 8-K filing dated February 22, 2023, names only the drug COVI-MSC and may be about another trial of the drug."], "cant_tell": ["We cannot tell the real reason why the trial was terminated beyond the registry's stated explanation of slow enrollment.", "The omission of trial progress in investor filings is not proof of any intent to mislead.", "The results due date is an approximation of the FDAAA deadline, which only applies to applicable clinical trials, a status that is not fully public, so this is never evidence that the sponsor broke the law.", "We cannot tell if results were published in conference abstracts, non-indexed journals, or company websites that may have been missed by our searches.", "Trials outside of the snapshot scope were only looked up live, or not at all."]}}

